- Cross-service state storage (Redis vs Postgres)
- Idempotent producers and event schemas
- Sign-in flow with rate limiting and 429s
- End-to-end verification under load

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo JS: acquire lock, publish event, then proceed
async function attemptSignIn(userId){
  const locked = await redis.get(`lockout:${userId}`);
  if (locked) return {ok:false, code:429};
  // check policy in Postgres (omitted)
  // on failure:
  await pubClient.send({ key:`lockout:${userId}`, value: 'locked', ... });
  await redis.set(`lockout:${userId}`, 'LOCKED', 'EX', 900);
  return {ok:false, code:403};
}
```

